title: Darwin App Sandbox Spike Implementation Plan
status: draft
created: 2026-10-31
author: adrian
approach: "Five milestones, each producing evidence rather than a shippable feature. M1 is the custom helper: a policy model that emits SBPL, applied with `sandbox_init`, then exec. M2 is the fixture, a Rust crate plus a hostile script that is the common workload for both prototypes. M3 is the nono prototype: the same requests expressed through `CapabilitySet`, with anything inexpressible recorded as a gap rather than worked around silently. M4 is lifecycle and egress: process groups, pause, resume, group kill, and a local server as the only network target. M5 writes the findings and the recommendation. No milestone touches the Litterbox CLI, its MCP surface, or any workspace crate."
architecture: "Two standalone binaries and one fixture, all under `adrs/2026-10-31-darwin-app-sandbox/poc`. Neither binary imports the other and neither imports Litterbox: the existing interface is Docker-shaped and is deliberately out of scope, so each prototype is free to express what its mechanism allows. Each binary takes `--workspace`, repeatable path and network grants, then `--` and a command. The custom binary builds SBPL from those arguments, applies it, and execs. The nono binary builds a `CapabilitySet`, applies it, and execs. Neither returns, because the process image is replaced by the confined child. The fixture runs as that child, so both prototypes confine the same workload.\n\n{{mermaid: architecture.mmd}}"
technologies[6]{name,role}:
  Rust 2021,Prototype language; both binaries and the fixture crate
  sandbox_init (libSystem),Applies an SBPL profile to the calling process
  SBPL,"Policy language for filesystem, network, mach and sysctl rules"
  nono 0.81,"Pinned candidate library; sandbox_init on macOS, Landlock on Linux"
  sandbox-exec,Cross-check for the same profiles and the documented fallback
  python3 http.server,Local egress target; no external network dependency
components[11]{name,purpose,details}:
  poc/custom,SBPL generation and application,"Owns a small policy model, renders it to SBPL, canonicalises every path before rendering, applies the profile with `sandbox_init`, then execs. Carries the deny-default baseline, the invariants the caller cannot override, and an empty network grant set. No dependency beyond libc. Covers FR-012 to FR-020 and AC-011 to AC-013."
  poc/nono,Same requests through nono,"Maps workspace and grants onto `CapabilitySet`, calls `Sandbox::apply_auto`, then execs. Records every request the capability model cannot express, with the reason. Raw `platform_rule` injection is used only to measure how far it reaches, and each use is listed as a gap. Covers FR-021 to FR-023 and AC-014."
  poc/fixture,Workload definition,"A Rust crate that builds and tests, plus a script that attempts a write outside the workspace, a read of `~/.ssh`, an outbound connection, and a child process that repeats the write. Identical for both prototypes so results are comparable. Covers FR-001, FR-003 and AC-001 to AC-005."
  poc/run.sh,Workload and hostile run,"Materialises the fixture into a workspace and runs build, test, run and the hostile checks under one prototype, exiting non-zero if any check leaks. Covers FR-003, FR-004 and AC-001 to AC-005."
  poc/lifecycle.sh,Lifecycle harness,"Pauses, resumes and group-kills a live loop, fails if the pid is not its own process-group leader, counts survivors by sentinel, and demonstrates the setsid escape. Covers FR-006 and AC-006 to AC-007."
  poc/egress.sh,Egress harness,"Starts local servers on ephemeral ports, probes the granted port, an ungranted port and name resolution, and reports the errno of each connect rather than a single denied word. Covers FR-015 and AC-004."
  poc/failclosed.sh,Fail-closed harness,"Runs the helper with invalid inputs, a symlink escape and a profile dump into the workspace, asserting the exact exit code and that the command never ran. Covers FR-020 and AC-008."
  poc/inside-home.sh,Credential harness,"Grants the whole home, places the workspace inside it, and checks that credential reads, keychain reads and traversal are denied while an ordinary home file stays readable. Covers FR-017 and AC-002."
  poc/ps-capture.sh,Process-table check,"Runs a resident command and asserts the profile text never appears in the process table while the command does. Covers AC-012."
  poc/timing.py,Cost measurement,"Times apply-plus-exec against a bare exec baseline, reporting median and p95. Covers NFR-004."
  findings.md,The deliverable,"Per question: observed behaviour, the exact profile or error, the gap, and the open risk for a production implementation. Written as findings are made, not reconstructed at the end. Covers FR-009, FR-010 and AC-010."
dataFlow: "The fixture runs as the confined child of whichever prototype is under test. The prototype parses arguments, canonicalises paths, constructs its policy, applies confinement, and execs; the child inherits the sandbox and cannot widen it. Observations are collected outside the sandbox: exit code, stderr, errno from the denied syscall, and whether the write landed on the host. Each observation is recorded with the profile that produced it. Nothing about the policy crosses a process boundary, because each binary both generates and applies its own."
deployment: "None. Both prototypes are throwaway binaries under the ADR directory, are not members of the Cargo workspace, and are referenced by no Litterbox crate. They are removed with the ADR once the findings are accepted."
